<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Mattia Egloff <mattia.egloff@pm.me>
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

Restore reads package sources from the *account's* NuGet.Config when the
repo has none. That made the build depend on ambient machine state: it
worked on GitLab's SaaS Windows images, which ship a default config, and
failed on pam with NU1100 for all 56 packages — Microsoft's own runtime
packs included — because a freshly provisioned account has no sources at
all (job 16461294262; `dotnet nuget list source` printed "No sources
found.", job 16461804947).

<clear /> makes the set explicit rather than inherited, so every runner
restores from the same place. The repo uses no private feed; if one is
ever added it belongs here, not in a box's user profile.
-->
<configuration>
  <packageSources>
    <clear />
    <add key="nuget.org" value="https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json" protocolVersion="3" />
  </packageSources>
</configuration>
